@      *$SET TRACE ASMLIST COPYLIST PARAS REF
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.   MPTZ024.
       AUTHOR.       PENNY GENOVESE.
       DATE-WRITTEN. FEBRUARY 26, 1992.
      *****************************************************************
      *SYSTEM NAME:   EDITORIAL SYSTEMS
      *APPL NAME:     OEM PARTS UPDATE
      *PROGRAM NAME:  MPTZ024 - SUPERSESSION UPDATE PROGRAM
      *LANGUAGE:      COBOL II / Oracle
      *DESCRIPTION:
      *  FUNCTION: THIS IS THE PARTS ORACLE UPDATE PGM WHICH PROCESSES
      *            THE SUPERSESSION TRANSACTIONS THAT ARE SUPPLIED BY
      *            THE OEM VIA A TAPE. INVALID TRANSACTION INFORMATION
      *            IS WRITTEN IN A ORACLE TABLE FOR LATER REPORTING.
      *            (NOTE - PROCESSED INFORMATION IS NOT RECORDED.)
      *
      *  INPUT:    CONTROL INFORMATION (PROGRAM PARM FILE)
      *            REFORMATTED TRANSACTION FILE
      *
      *  I/O:      ORACLE OEM TABLE
      *            ORACLE PARTS TABLES
      *            ORACLE CEG LINE TABLE
      *            ORACLE WIP LINE TABLE
      *            ORACLE ALTERNATE PARTS TABLE
      *            ORACLE REPORT TABLE
      *            ORACLE RESTART TABLE
      *
      *  OUTPUT:   DATABASE UPDATE CONTROL REPORT
      *
      * SIGNIFICANT PROCESSING NARRATIVE:
      *   PROGRAM USES A CONTROL FILE TO DETERMINE WHICH OEM IS BEING
      *   PROCESSED AND FOR WHAT EFFECTIVE DATE. THE EFFECTIVE DATE
      *   MUST BE GREATER THAN THE LAST SUPER DATE W/I THE OEM TABLE.
      *
      *   1) VALIDATES CONTROL FILE PARAMETERS.
      *   2) CHECK IF RESTART ROW FOUND INDICATING RESTART RUN
      *   3) READS TRANS RECORD AND VALIDATES OLD AND NEW PART #.
      *         (IF PRIOR SUPERSESSION, TALLIES BUT DOES NOT REPORT
      *         TRANS AS ERROR. IF OTHER TYPE OF ERROR, INSERTS ERROR
      *         REPORT ROW IN THE REPORT TABLE.)
      *   4) SUPERSESSION ROW IS INSERTED
      *   5) IF VALID TRANSACTION AND PART IS IN PARTS TABLE,
      *         SUPERSESSION IS PERFORMED.
      *      NEW PART IS INSERTED
      *      ALL LINES ASSOCIATED TO OLD PART ARE CONNECTED TO NEW PART
      *      OLD PART IS DELETED
      *   6) AT END OF RUN, CONTROL REPORT IS PRODUCED SHOWING Oracle
      *         table ACTIVITY AND TRANSACTION ACTIVITY
      *
      *   *  COMMITS PERFORMED EVERY 5000 ROWS (LIMIT IS SET IN WRK STG)
      *   *  RESTART ROWS WRITTEN AT EACH COMMIT POINT. (AT SUCCESSFUL
      *         END, IT IS DELETED.))
      *   *  PROCESSED SUPERSESSIONS AREN'T REPORTED.
      *
      * CALLED PROGRAMS:
      *    CALL "dberrmsg" USING SQLCA ERROR-MESSAGE ERROR-LENGTH.
      *
      * CONTROL CARD:
      *  (SAME CONTROL CARD THAT'S USED IN THE UPDATE PROGRAMS)
      *
      *  OEM=XXX,REGN=X,EFFDT=XX/XX/XXXX,REPLACE=X,RUNTYP=XXX,
      *       1       2           3              4         5
      *
      *  NAGSTYP=XXXXXXXX
      *             6
      *
      *       1 - NUMERIC; OEM NUMBER WHICH YOU ARE PROCESSING
      *
      *       2 - ALPHA; REGION OF THE OEM (U = US, C = CAN)
      *
      *       3 - NUMERIC; PRICE EFFECTIVE DATE AS SPECIFIED BY THE
      *           OEM  (FORMAT MM/DD/YYYY; MUST BE GREATER THAN LAST RUN
      *           UNLESS THIS IS REPLACEMENT RUN - THEN MUST = LAST RUN)
      *
      *       4 - ALPHA; REPLACEMENT INDICATOR (FOR PRICE UPDATE PGM);
      *           (N = NEW RUN, PRICES WILL BE UPDATED - CURRENT MOVED
      *           TO PREVIOUS THEN TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED TO CURRENT;
      *           Y = REPLACEMENT RUN, TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED DIRECTLY
      *           OVER CURRENT PRICE; USED FOR CORRECTING MISPRICING.)
      *
      *       5 - ALPHA; TYPE OF RUN (OEM = OEM, SUP = SUPPLIMENTAL)
      *           (USED BY REPORT PROGRAM MPTZ007)
      *
      *       6 - ALPHA; TYPE OF NAGS RUN (FOR NAGS RUN, EITHER "IMPORT"
      *           OR "DOMESTIC"; ANY OTHER RUNS, "N/A")
      *           (PRINTED IN HEADING - JUST TO DISTINGUISH BETWEEN THE
      *            IMPORT AND DOMESTIC RUN REPORTS)
      *
      * MODIFICATION LOG:
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 01/23/2019  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
