      *                   CALL TO SUPERSEDE PARTS IN THE PART TRACKER
      *                   TABLE.
      * --------------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/21/01 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: RACE II REVISIONS:
      *                1. ADDED NEW ABEND PARAGRAPH AND CODE FOR PROCEDURE
      *                   CALLS.  PARAGRAPH:Y1500
      * --------------------------------------------------------------------
      * 12/05/00 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: RACE II REVISIONS:
      *                1. CONVERTED FOR NEW ERD STRUCTURE AND
      *                   PART TABLE DEFAULTS
      *                2. ADDED INITIALIZE FOR RETURNED VARIABLES
      *                   IN SELECT PROCEDURE CALLS
      * --------------------------------------------------------------------
      * 07/19/00 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: RACE II REVISIONS:
      *                1. CONVERTED FOR NEW DATABASE STRUCTURE
      *                2. CONVERTED EMBEDDED SQL TO PACKAGE/PROCEDURE CALLS
      * ---------------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/08/2000  BY:  KIM DINH
      *           DESC:  ADD CURR_EFF_DT TO ALL QUERIES THAT ACCESS
      *                  IIST001 AND IIST002 TABLES
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 03/11/99  BY:   JOHN CUSUMANO
      *           DESC: RACE - VERSIONING
      *                 REPLACE FLAT RATE CODE. INCLUDE PROCESSING OF
      *                 WIP TABLE WMCGT003
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/26/98  BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *           DESC: REMOVE ALL REFERENCES TO 'UK' AND SPECIAL
      *                 CANADIAN OEM NUMBERS.  CONVERT FROM LOWER
      *                 TO UPPER CASE.
      *
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 03/28/97  BY:   Al Faelschle
      *           DESC: Removed moves to ws-paragraph in abend routines.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/15/96  BY:   Al Faelschle
      *           DESC: Converted from MVS and DB2 to Unix and Oracle
      *                 for Rehost project.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 09/07/96  BY:   STEVE CARROLL
      *           DESC: REMOVE ALL REFERENCES TO THE INTERCHANGE DB.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/28/95  BY:   PATTY BECOTTE
      *           DESC: CHANGED TO CHECK 'NAGSTYP' FOR 'N/A'. IF SO, DO
      *                 NOT PRINT, ELSE MOVE VALUE IN CNTL-NAGS-TYP TO
      *                 HEADING.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 01/20/95  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: CHG'D RESTART LOGIC TO USE MULTIPLE RESTART RECS
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 08/31/94  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: 1) CHANGED PERFORM OF SUPER LOOP TO BE BASED ON
      *                    MEDT001.SUPER_BY_DT_FL (WHETHER OEM USES DATE
      *                    TO FOLLOW SUPER CHAIN).
      *                 2) ALL SUPERS THAT ARE NOT EITHER "PRIOR" OR
      *                    "ALREADY SUPE" WILL BE INSERTED TO THE DB
      *                    (WHETHER DATED OR NOT - SEE 11/15/93 #5).
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 04/07/94  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: 1) CHANGED UPDATE OF ASSOC. LINE TABLES TO NOT
      *                    UPDATE LST_UPDT_DT.
      *                 2) CHANGED COUNT OF CEG LINE CHANGES TO OMIT
      *                    IMPACT TO FRWD POINTED LINES.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 03/08/94  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: ADDED LOGIC TO CHECK IF NEW PART SUPERSEDES TO
      *                 ANOTHER PART (EFFECTIVE TODAY OR IN FUTURE) SO
      *                 THAT LINES ARE POINTED TO MOST RECENT PART W/I
      *                 THE SUPERSESSION CHAIN.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/15/93  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: PROGRAM CREATED FROM MPTZ004.
      *                 1) TRANS FILE INCREASED FROM 51 TO 100 BYTES.
      *                    (OLD VERSION STILL REQUIRED FOR OEM'S THAT
      *                    HAVEN'T BEEN CONVERTED TO NEW FORMAT YET.)
      *                 2) CHANGED SEARCH OF PRIOR SUPERSESSION TO
      *                    INCL. FOLLOWING CHAIN. (IF SUPERSEDING PART
      *                    NUM AT END-OF-CHAIN EQUALS TRANS NEW PART
      *                    THEN "PRIOR SUPERSESSION".)
      *                 3) SUPERSESSION WILL NOW BE DATED FROM TRANS REC
      *                    (UNLESS TRANS DATE IS BLANK; THEN USES PARM).
      *                 4) DATED TRANSACTIONS THAT DO NOT HAVE PARTS IN
      *                    THE DATABASE WILL BE ADDED TO THE SUPER TBL.
      *                    (THEY USED TO BE BYPASSED AS 'PART NOT ON
      *                    DB'.)
      *                 5) NOT DATED SUPERSESSIONS THAT CONTINUE
      *                    EXISTING CHAINS WILL CONTINUE TO BE ADDED TO
      *                    THE SUPERSESSION TABLE.
      *                 6) BUILD SUPERSEDED PART ROW W/ ZERO PRICE, NULL
      *                    DATE (WAS BUILDING IT FROM "OLD" PART INFO.)
      * ---------------------------------------------------------------
      * 07/30/26  BY:   RODRIGO JASINSKI - rj132422
      *           DESC: AIX to RHEL conversion
      ******************************************************************
