             PERFORM Y1500-SQL-PROCEDURE-ERROR THRU Y1500-EXIT.


       R2300-EXIT. EXIT.

      ****************************************************************
      * R2400-UPDATE-PART-DATA:                                      *
      *     RACE II - NEW ROUTINE                                    *
      *  IF THE NEW PART IS NOT IN THE DB, BUILD THE NEW PART DATA   *
      *  IN THE OLD PART ROW, REUSING THE OLD PART SKEY AND CREATING *
      *  AN AUTOMATIC SUPERSESSION.                                  *
      *  THE PART SKEY REPRESENTS THE NATIVE KEY:                    *
      *    PART-SUPPLIER, PART-SUPPLIER-COUNTRY-ABBR, PART-NUMBER    *
      *  REPLACES R2100-INSERT-NEW-PART (FOR NEW SUPERSESSION)       *
      ****************************************************************
       R2400-UPDATE-PART-DATA.
           MOVE "R2400-UPDATE-PART-DATA" TO WS-PARAGRAPH.
           MOVE WS-PARAGRAPH TO WS-PARNAME.
           MOVE "PART" TO WS-TBLNAME.
           MOVE "UPDATE" TO WS-FUNCTION.

